# Repository-root environment example — comments only, no real values.
#
# No secrets belong in source control. Per-app examples with the full variable lists:
#   apps/web/.env.example        (browser-visible values only; nothing secret)
#   services/voice/.env.example  (server-side keys: Gnani / Gemini / Supabase)
#
# Playwright (npm run test:e2e) targets this origin for the web app.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000 when unset.
# PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# The voice service health entry point:
#   SPEAKING_COACH_SERVICE_URL  (scripts/foundation/service-health-check.mjs)
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000 when unset.
# SPEAKING_COACH_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
# The browser-origin allowlist of the voice service (Phase 03 FIX-1). One
# list, two jobs: the CORS allowlist of the HTTP routes and the allowlist
# of the WebSocket handshake. A JSON array or a comma-separated list; the
# wildcard "*" is refused while the settings parse.
#   SPEAKING_COACH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS  (services/voice/.env.example)
# Defaults to the local web origin only: http://localhost:3000
#
# The browser-visible voice service URL (Phase 03 FIX-1). It is NOT a
# secret and it is the only NEXT_PUBLIC_ value in this repository:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_VOICE_WS_URL  (apps/web/.env.example)
# Defaults to ws://localhost:8000/ws/call
#
# Supabase (Phase 06). The publishable key is read server-side only; never
# put it behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
#
# Phase 07. The assembled suite (`npm run test:assembled`) uses its own fake
# Supabase and provider ports; it reads no credential. The latency endpoint
# and the resource guards are configured in services/voice/.env.example.
# The live harness is opt-in and billable:
#   GNANI_LIVE_TESTS=1 GNANI_API_KEY=... GEMINI_API_KEY=... GEMINI_MODEL=...
#   uv run --project services/voice python -m pytest tests/integration/live -q -s
# Operations, limits and what is still fake-proven: docs/operations/RUNBOOK.md
